  {
   "n": 3,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Recall that a Turing Machine T can be represented or ‘coded’ by an integer <em>m</em>. Let us write ‘the <em>m</em><sup>th</sup> Turing Machine’ to mean the Turing Machine coded by <em>m</em>. Which of the following sets is not recursively enumerable?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>The set of <em>m</em> such that the <em>m</em><sup>th</sup> Turing Machine halts on the input 0.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>The set of <em>m</em> such that the <em>m</em><sup>th</sup> Turing Machine does not halt on the input 0.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>The set of <em>m</em> such that the <em>m</em><sup>th</sup> Turing Machine halts on the input <em>m</em>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>The set of <em>n</em> such that all Turing Machines halt on the input <em>n</em>.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(b)</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c1/c17afa3a98eb0bac0ade.png\" /></p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. If a language L is finite, then the minimal DFA accepting <em>L</em> contains no cycle.<br />\n2. Every DFA accepting a finite language must contain a dead state.<br />\nWhich of the above statements are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Only 1"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Only 2"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Both 1 and 2"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Neither 1 nor 2"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(b)</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d863f735b09943b1dcd2.png\" /></p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : There exist no algorithm for deciding if any two Turing Machine M1 and M2 accept the same language.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : The problem of determining whether a Turing Machine halts on any input is undecidable.<br />\nWhich one of the following options is correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> are correct</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> are not correct</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is correct</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a)<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Equivalence test of two TM is undecidable.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Halting problem of TM is undecidable.</p>"
  },
