  {
   "n": 11,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>Which of the following problems are decidable?</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cce97b0dc437bacc6329.png\" /></p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "1, 2, 3, 4"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "1, 2"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "2, 3, 4"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "3, 4"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>(d)<br />\nCFL&rsquo;s are not closed under complementation and a program can loop forever. So, it may not produce any output.<br />\nRegular and recursive languages are closed under complementation.<br />\nHence, only 3, 4 are decidable.</p>"
  },
